# Shared Emscripten link flags for sim_core WASM (Makefile + CMakeLists.txt).
# One flag per line. Lines starting with # are ignored.
# Optimization (-O3 / -O0) is applied by each build driver, not here.
# Release-only flags (-g0) live in the `wasm` Makefile target instead, since
# `wasm-dbg` needs the opposite — see cpp/README.md for the full mapping.
#
# No JS glue, no Embind (#254 §3): `make wasm` writes sim_core.wasm alone, a
# standalone reactor module (--no-entry) that exports the flat C ABI in
# cpp/src/sim_core_abi.cpp (generated from cpp/abi.json) plus its memory.
# src/wasm/sim-core/instantiate.ts supplies its two imports and
# abi.generated.ts wraps the exports — that is the whole JS ⇄ WASM surface.
# The export list is the codegen's, not hand-kept: generated/sim-core-exports.json.
--no-entry
-sSTANDALONE_WASM=1
-sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS=@../generated/sim-core-exports.json
# 4 MiB, growing on demand: the particle buffer is a std::vector sized at
# seedParticles() (it used to be a 1.6 MB inline array in every
# SEGSimulator), so most realms never grow. The page, the plant worker and
# the offline worker each instantiate one; 16 MiB × 3 was the old floor.
-sALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1
-sINITIAL_MEMORY=4194304
-sMALLOC=emmalloc
-sFILESYSTEM=0
-fno-exceptions
